   174	    Input structure:
   175	    - A black background contains several disconnected monochrome objects with pairwise distinct colors.
   176	    - Exactly one gray single pixel marks the spiral origin and is not part of any object.
   177	    - Objects may lie on different spiral rings, and edge clipping can remove parts of the infinite spiral path.
   178	
   179	    Rule:
   180	    - Start at the gray marker and traverse an outward square spiral cell by cell with the fixed order up, right, down, left and step lengths 1, 1, 2, 2, 3, 3, ...
   181	    - Ignore spiral positions that fall outside the grid, but keep the same global traversal order.
   182	    - Record the first time each object is touched by the spiral, then recolor every object with the previous object's original color in that order, wrapping the first object to the last object's color.
